FireCREST v2: expose what portals need to chart jobs and the cluster

- Job submission takes the resource requests sbatch would read from #SBATCH
  lines (nodes, minimum_nodes, tasks, tasks_per_node, cpus_per_task,
  memory_per_node, time_limit). slurmrestd does not parse #SBATCH, so without
  them every job runs with the partition defaults.
- Jobs report time.submission, time.totalCpu (accounting), allocationCpus,
  requestedMemory and maxRss (largest step peak RSS, accounting).
- Nodes are read through SlurmNode, mapping free_mem, alloc_idle_cpus and the
  drain/down reason.
- Reservations report partition, nodeCount and flags (e.g. MAINT), and no
  longer require a "Features" key.
- Job listings accept a 30-day window ("30d") for history charts.

